# No static helper functions

Static helper functions are considered poor style in this project ("wiocha").

## Prefer instead
- `extension` on the relevant type (e.g. `String.decodingHTMLEntities`)
- Instance methods when behavior belongs to an object
- Injected dependencies / protocols when behavior may need swapping or mocking

## Avoid
- `private static func` utility helpers on view models / services
- `Self.someHelper(...)` call sites for pure transforms that belong on the value type

## Allowed exceptions
- True type factories (`static func make...` returning `Self`) when that is the clearest API
- Framework-required entry points
